 single managed node, with a clear pre-restart baseline, acknowledgement, changed boot identity (corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots), and recovered sshd/certificate state. Minor unremoved temp files (/tmp/test_known_hosts, /tmp/reboot.log) are the only notable hygiene issue.\",\"limitations\":[\"Cluster/data-state recovery is not applicable beyond sshd since this task and topology involve a single non-clustered node; only service-level (sshd) and configuration-level (CA/cert files) recovery could be observed.\",\"The 'Permission denied (publickey,password,keyboard-interactive)' seen in both connection tests is expected given BatchMode/no valid client key, and evidence relies on interpreting the preceding debug lines correctly to confirm host verification succeeded independent of that failure.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ca-created","requirement":"Create an SSH certificate authority on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"An ed25519 CA keypair was generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca with a directory permission of 700, directly observed via ssh-keygen output and directory listing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99bb780812304a4c"]},{"id":"host-cert-signed-presented","requirement":"Host presents a certificate signed by the CA","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node1 ed25519 host key was signed by the CA (ssh-keygen -s) producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with correct CA fingerprint and principals; sshd_config was updated with a HostCertificate directive, validated with sshd -t, and sshd was restarted successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9774ee0623354d04","cmd-9ca4109497674518","cmd-8387c01f04d6420c"]},{"id":"client-trust-no-pinning","requirement":"A client that trusts the CA (without pinning the host key) connects without a host-key mismatch/prompt","status":"satisfied","summary":"A known_hosts file containing only an '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' line (no pinned host key) was used with StrictHostKeyChecking=yes; ssh debug output shows the se